{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Holding","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV7HoldingV","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"extendedModule":"Gnusto","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","title":"GameText.Holding","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Holding","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding\/holder","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding\/item"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding\/samples"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Holding","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one"}]},{"type":"text","text":" object, and a sentence about two needs some way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to say which is which. The roles are a type rather than a pair, because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pair spelling — a tuple, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$1"},{"type":"text","text":" — leaves the API unable to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answer the only question an author actually asks at the call site: which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one is the container? "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\($0.holder)"},{"type":"text","text":" answers it; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\($1)"},{"type":"text","text":" does not."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One struct serves every line whose two things stand in this relation,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than one apiece — which is also what lets ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RoomDescriber"},{"text":" keep","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handing ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemOnSurface","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemInContainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one helper as a value. Another such line should cost no edit here.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"Line","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over one of these is ","type":"text"},{"code":"ExpressibleByStringLiteral","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two-object line will take a fixed sentence — ","type":"text"},{"code":"text.putItemIn = \"Done.\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— and print it without either name. For these that is a legitimate thing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for a game to want, and the sentence it prints is still true. It is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"legitimate for a line whose whole content is the thing it was handed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is why these are ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DroppableSubject","type":"reference"},{"text":"s and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Word","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its neighbours are not.","type":"text"}]},{"code":["text.putItemIn = .naming { \"You tuck \\($0.item) into \\($0.holder).\" }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both arrive as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Noun","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the reason one does — and for a second reason","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a one-object line never has. A sentence about two things has two things","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its verb might agree with, and it is rarely the one the sentence names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/itemOnSurface","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads “On the table are the rails”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where the verb agrees with the rails and the template names the table.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"While these were a pair of strings there was no way to write that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sentence at all.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Holding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A thing and what holds it: what the player put down, and the box, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"table or the hamper it went into.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DroppableSubject","doc:\